    "title": "LEGION BASEBALL: Sixers go hitless in Northwest Regional opener | Cheyenne Post 6 | wyomingnews.com",
    "text": "CHEYENNE – The Cheyenne Sixers were held to just two base runners and no hits during the American Legion Northwest Regional Tournament opener against Honolulu, Hawaii's Team Central on Wednesday afternoon in Medford, Oregon.\nCheyenne surrendered seven runs in the fifth inning to fall 12-0.\nCatcher Brayden Kamarad and second baseman Colin Crecelius were the only Sixers to reach base in the game, both coming off walks in the third and fourth innings.\nThe loss drops Cheyenne to the loser's bracket. It faces the loser of the Missoula Mavericks and Medford Mustangs in an elimination game Thursday, which is slated to take place 30 minutes after the 10:30 a.m. game.",
    "summary": "CHEYENNE – The Cheyenne Sixers were held to just two base runners and no hits during the American Legion Northwest Regional Tournament opener against Honolulu, Hawaii's Team Central on Wednesday afternoon in Medford, Oregon. Cheyenne surrendered seven runs in the fifth inning to fall 12-0. Catcher Brayden Kamarad and second baseman Colin Crecelius were the only Sixers to reach base in the game, both coming off walks in the third and fourth innings. The loss drops Cheyenne to the loser's bracket.",
